      "message": "This fixes a real EAS \"issue\" but it does it in a WALT centri way by also adding yet another CONFIG_SCHED_WALT guard in fair.c.\n\nA better solution would be to make a better usage of the cpu_util_wake() both in group_max_util() and group_norm_util().\nIndeed, cpu_util_wake() already knows about WALT not accouting for blocked load, and using its returned value it becomes easier to just add back the task_util to the src or dst CPU, depending whether we are in the before or the after case.\n\nWe already have a couple of patches which implements this more generic solution, which is thus worth to post for review as a possible alternative to this one.",
